      "message": "Runtime control of host command logging using `hcdebug` is no longer a requirement for any FAFT tests.  Originally, there was a FAFT test `firmware_ECBootTime` that used the \"HC\" output on the EC console and also called `hcdebug`.  However, when this test got converted to [tast](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/tast-tests/src/go.chromium.org/tast-tests/cros/remote/bundles/cros/firmware/boot_time.go;l\u003d58) it now only checks for the AP reaching S0.\n\nI\u0027m in favor of dropping the runtime support completely when using the upstream CONFIG_EC_HOST_CMD.\n\nUpstream, you should just use Zephyr\u0027s logging.  The developer can select a build time log level by setting `CONFIG_EC_HC_LOG_LEVEL_DBG`.",
